{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This article describes the KeyboardKit styling engine."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Styling-Article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit’s various views can be customized to great extent, with custom view builders and style- & behavior-related view modifiers."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Assets","anchor":"Assets"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit defines keyboard-specific "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/Color","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/Image","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/Font","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" extensions, like "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/Color\/keyboardBackground","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/Image\/keyboardNewline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/Font\/keyboardFont","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", to make it easy to create keyboards that look like a native iO